BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Ben UFO Open - Close at Mooi Space presented by Standard Time x PA
 RADOX
DTSTART:20260911T220000
DTEND:20260911T220000
UID:eb528152a162282eef93593759f87085@yohomo.ca
DESCRIPTION:Known for making the “experimental accessible”\, Ben UFO i
 s a British DJ\, radio host and cofounder of the label Hessle Audio – ho
 me to artists such as Shanti Celeste\, Pangaea and Call Super. His knowled
 ge of multiple forms of bass music\, from garage\, jungle and DnB to techn
 o and house\, shows up in his all-encompassing DJ sets\, which have “no 
 regard for geographical or chronological borders” Ben UFO Open to Close 
 at Mooi Space presented by Standard Time x Paradox Ben UFO: (Open to Close
  Room 1) 747 b2b Emily Nicoll (Room 2) Caleb Klager (Live Room 2) This eve
 nt will also be hosting the Black Sunflowers TIFF premiere afterparty No p
 hotos / video Room 1: Over the past five years\, Ben UFO has acquired a de
 served reputation as one of contemporary dance music’s most daring and w
 ide-ranging selectors\, with his keen ear and razor-sharp technical abilit
 ies enabling him to cut between eras\, lineages and mixing styles with daz
 zling ease and fluidity. Having cut his teeth in early dubstep and drum 
 ’n’ bass\, his roots lie in UK rave culture – yet his selections cas
 t the net wider\, drawing new mutations of this culture into the orbit of 
 house\, techno and other global dancefloor sounds. In the club\, his sets 
 somehow manage to be simultaneously considered and raucous\, sliding from 
 sidewinding broken rhythms into an irresistible four-to-the-floor groove\,
  or broadsiding you with unexpected tangents\, old favourites and bizarre 
 secret weapons. It’s refreshingly difficult to pin down what makes Ben
 ’s DJing distinctive and exciting\, whether you encounter it on the radi
 o\, in a recorded mix or on the dancefloor. If there’s a core characteri
 stic of his approach it’s an infectious warmth and restless love of expl
 oration\, exemplified by his habit of meshing mind-bendingly strange track
 s into peak-time sets\, and by the way his Thursday night shows on Rinse F
 M weave together jacking unreleased dance cuts with new finds and dubbed-o
 ut oddities from across the globe. In the club\, he shapes these elements 
 into something rich and unpredictable\, interspersing phases of driving mo
 mentum with joyful curveballs and ruptures in the flow that jolt you back 
 to your senses — moments\, as he describes it\, that feel like coming up
  for air on the dancefloor. From their early years in Leeds\, Ben UFO and 
 Hessle Audio have evolved into core figures in an increasingly globally-co
 nnected dance music scene. Having provided an early platform for music fro
 m kindred innovative spirits such as Blawan\, Peverelist\, Untold and Joe\
 , the label continues to release new music from both its founders and emer
 ging new artists. This openness marks the cornerstone of Ben’s approach:
  drawing connections\, exploring new ideas\, and feeding some of Hessle Au
 dio’s energy and enthusiasm back into the musical communities of which t
 hey are an integral part. Room 2: Paradox curates a lineup of Toronto&#x27
 \;s staple underground artists. The kind of names that mean everything to 
 those who&#x27\;ve been paying attention. 747 and Emily Nicoll jopen the n
 ight for a extended b2b . Co-founders of the highly regarded Aquaregia lab
 el\, and with 747&#x27\;s sets having resonated across some of the world&#
 x27\;s most celebrated clubs and institutions\, this is an opening that de
 mands your attention from the first record. Closing out the night\, Caleb 
 Klager takes the floor for a live hardware set. An artist spoken about in 
 hushed tones by those who know. Consistently pushing the boundaries of sou
 nd and leaving the room inspired. ‍
LOCATION:Mooi\, 75 Pelham Ave
URL:https://www.yohomo.ca/event/ben-ufo-open---close-at-mooi-space-present
 ed-by-standard-time-x-paradox
X-SOURCE:YOHOMO
END:VEVENT
