DESCRIPTION:Join our Generations for Climate Justice program for a communi
 ty nature walk on Saturday\, September 12\, from 1 to 3 p.m. at Toronto&#x
 27\;s Evergreen Brick Works [550 Bayview Ave]. The walk is for 2SLGBTQ+ co
 mmunity members of all ages. Together\, we&#x27\;ll learn more about the l
 and we&#x27\;re on\, make connections\, and take in nature&#x27\;s beauty.
  The event is free\, and RSVP is required. Save your spot at: The519.org/G
 CJwalk For questions or to share access needs\, Email Erin EOBrien@The519.
 org. Generations for Climate Justice (GCJ) is a free program that connects
  2SLGBTQ+ youth (ages 10 to 18) and 2SLGBTQ+ older adults (ages 50+) to bu
 ild impactful intergenerational relationships and foster collaboration on 
 climate justice projects. Thanks to @priderunto for supporting this progra
 m. [Image description: A group of people walking up an inclined path in a 
 forested area. Text below reads: &quot\;Community Nature Walk with Generat
 ions for Climate Justice. Saturday\, September 12\, 1 to 3 p.m. at Evergre
 en Brick Works [550 Bayview Ave.]&quot\;. Logo of pride &amp\; remembrance
  run.] ‍
