BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Queer Death Salon: Grief Gardening
DTSTART:20260929T190000
DTEND:20260929T190000
UID:40cd6071e9f334c36d15928b27c42d6a@yohomo.ca
DESCRIPTION:In times of grief\, many people find that a connection to land
 \, earth\, and the tending of life can help carry us through. It is well e
 stablished that a connection to nature\, no matter how small\, helps impro
 ve our experiences of depression\, anxiety\, and sense of wellbeing. Pulli
 ng from their their personal experiences\, Eli will lead participants in a
  discussion about\; the history of Grief Gardening through various cultura
 l perspectives gardening as a tool for emotional processing and providing 
 a sense of control and purpose creating sites for remembrance tending to a
  relationship with nature to encourage a sense of hope and renewal He will
  also support participants with ideas about how to get started or expand o
 n our grief gardens. Eli (they/he) is a gardener and former landscaper\, w
 etlands restorationist and wildlife biologist currently living on Ohlone l
 and in Oakland. Mutual aid\, covid realism\, disability justice\, queernes
 s and art as well as gardening all help them with the little and big sourc
 es of grief that life brings us. ‍
LOCATION:Online\, online
URL:https://www.yohomo.ca/event/queer-death-salon-grief-gardening
X-SOURCE:YOHOMO
END:VEVENT
